# {{.Slug}}

Scheduled report. Cron fires (default 9am weekdays), fetches metrics
from an HTTP endpoint, posts a one-line summary to a Slack-compatible
chat webhook.

Generated by `reactor new scheduled-report {{.Slug}}` on {{.Date}}.

## Prerequisites

```bash
reactor vault add --name metrics-api-key --provider shared-secret --value $METRICS_BEARER
reactor vault add --name chat-webhook-url --provider shared-secret --value $SLACK_WEBHOOK
reactor vault grant --workflow {{.Slug}} --credential metrics-api-key
reactor vault grant --workflow {{.Slug}} --credential chat-webhook-url
```

## Run it locally

```bash
reactor workflow build --src . --slug {{.Slug}}
reactor workflow register --db sqlite://./reactor.db --slug {{.Slug}} --src main.go
reactor serve --db sqlite://./reactor.db
```

In the dashboard at `/workflows/{{.Slug}}` click "Add cron trigger" with
spec `0 9 * * 1-5` (or your own schedule) + optional IANA timezone.

## How replay works

The wall-clock stamp goes through `reactor.SideEffect` so a retry sees
the cached value instead of "now at retry time"; the idempotency key
on both side-effecting steps is derived from the day so duplicate
firings on the same day are no-ops.
